            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0983" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1153 St 2/104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hammond</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-24T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 24—2:39
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>78. Referring to my telegram number 59, June 9, 11 a.m.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d735-f1"/> I am informed by Wescott, Shell representative, that he
                    has been instructed to accept a settlement of company’s claims for
                    expropriations on the basis of actual physical valuation, plus eight per cent,
                    plus legal interest from date of seizure. The Shell group has renounced its
                    endeavors to obtain compensation for good will and settlement on more favorable
                    exchange basis.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hammond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
